<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF corrects Oct Zambia copper import figure.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF corrects Oct Zambia copper import figure.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) has corrected a figure released last month for October refined copper imports from Zambia, a ministry official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The official said Japan imported 4,932 tonnes of copper from Zambia in October and not 105,222 tonnes as reported last month.</p>
<p>The correction will not appear in the ministry's cumulative year-to-date import data, however, until the scheduled release of the December data in late January, he said.</p>
<p>The corrected data means Japan's copper imports in October totalled 30,267 tonnes, up 19.3 percent from the year-ago period, instead of 130,557 tonnes, up 414.63 percent, as reported in late November.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
